{"files": [{"id": 47099674, "name": "ppat.1011970.g007.tif", "size": 1185012, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/47099674", "supplied_md5": "e5e4c21f03ccf7100351e1ef73fc6085", "computed_md5": "e5e4c21f03ccf7100351e1ef73fc6085", "mimetype": "image/tiff"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 4308, "full_name": "Yan Chen", "first_name": "Yan", "last_name": "Chen", "is_active": false, "url_name": "Yan_Chen", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841048, "full_name": "Rodney P. Kincaid", "first_name": "Rodney P.", "last_name": "Kincaid", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841051, "full_name": "Kelley Bastin", "first_name": "Kelley", "last_name": "Bastin", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841054, "full_name": "Devin N. Fachko", "first_name": "Devin N.", "last_name": "Fachko", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 18841057, "full_name": "Rebecca L. Skalsky", "first_name": "Rebecca L.", "last_name": "Skalsky", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/Abrogation_of_SOS1_limits_the_enhanced_lytic_reactivation_by_miR-142_knockdown_/26051941", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>A. RNAi-mediated inhibition of SOS1 attenuates EBV lytic gene expression in response to BCR crosslinking. miR-142 mutant MutuI 10024.C19 cells were stably transduced with empty vector control (pLCE) or shRNA against SOS1 and treated with anti-IgM for 0 or 24 hrs. Immunoblots were performed on lysates for lytic gene products and for Sos1 as knockdown validation. Gapdh levels are shown as loading controls. Shown is the representative of three independent experiments. B. Inhibition of SOS1 reduces activation of the Ras/Raf/Mek/Erk pathway. Time course of Mek/Erk pathway proteins by immunoblot in miR-142 mutant MutuI cells transduced with empty vector (pLCE) or shSOS1 following anti-IgM treatment. Gapdh levels are shown as loading controls. C. and D. Band intensities in panels A. and B. were quantified using ImageJ, normalized to loading controls, and reported relative to pLCE control cells. Shown are averages of at least three experiments. By Student\u2019s t-test, *p<0.05. E. Chemical inhibition of Sos1 attenuates EBV lytic gene expression. EBV lytic proteins were tested by immunoblot in miR-142 mutant MutuI cells pre-treated the Sos1 inhibitor BI-3406 for 24 hrs, followed by anti-IgM treatment for 24 hrs. Gapdh levels are shown as loading controls. F. Erk phosphorylation is reduced in the presence of the Sos1 chemical inhibitor. Time course of Erk proteins tested by immunoblot in miR-142 mutant MutuI cells pre-treated with the Sos1 inhibitor BI-3406 for 24 hrs, followed by anti-IgM treatment for indicated times. Gapdh levels are shown as loading controls. G. Model of how miR-142 regulates induction of EBV lytic gene expression through the Sos1/Ras/Raf/Mek/Erk signaling cascade.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 1185012, "created_date": "2024-06-17T17:37:31Z", "modified_date": "2024-06-28T17:35:38Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["b cell receptor", "surface ig cross", "xlink \"> reactivation", "142 targets related", "142 enhanced levels", "restricts ebv entry", "support viral infection", "infected bl cells", "cells using anti", "ebv lytic phase", "erk signaling initiated", "ebv reactivation", "mapk signaling", "lytic stage", "ig antibodies", "induce reactivation", "ebv latency", "taken together", "significant role", "results show", "latency plays", "key regulator", "immediate early", "grna library", "genetic ablation", "gain insight", "fully understood", "effects could", "dabrafenib ).", "clip 